# Documentation
docs/
# ...EXCEPT the three handoff directories the CODE reads at runtime.
#
# `sentinel/controller/frozen_rule.py` LOADS its thresholds from
# FROZEN_SENTINEL_1P1_RULE.json and verifies them against SHA256SUMS.txt — it
# raises FrozenRuleMissing rather than falling back to transcribed constants —
# and tests/sentinel's controller certification reads the frozen oracle tapes.
#
# Without these negations the test image collects an ImportError, and
# `sentinel-certify.sh` discovers it at STEP 5, after step 4's hours-long
# re-seed. The script's own step 2b says a refusal is only a refusal if it comes
# before the irreversible step; this keeps that true for a dependency added
# after it was written.
#
# NARROW ON PURPOSE: 3.6M of the handoff's 16M. The PDFs, prospectuses and
# source archives are evidence for humans and no code reads them.
!docs/sentinel-handoff/00_README/
!docs/sentinel-handoff/02_SENTINEL_1P1_FROZEN_ORACLE/
!docs/sentinel-handoff/04_BREADTH_ORACLES/

# The recovered breadth classifier, read by the TEST image only —
# `test_breadth_classifier.py` differentially checks `sentinel/breadth/` against
# it. The production module reads neither directory at runtime, so these are
# absent from the runtime image and must stay absent.
!docs/sentinel-breadth-reconstruction/
!docs/sentinel-reference-implementation/

# Certification-input records inspected and hashed from the clean test image.
# Keep these exceptions narrow: the rest of docs/ is human evidence and does
# not belong in an image build context.
!docs/f92c0cc-safety-reconstruction.md
!docs/main-review-remediation.md
!docs/production-certification-separation.md
!docs/sentinel-deployment.md
!docs/sentinel-paper-activation.md
!docs/sentinel-paper-observation.md
!docs/sentinel-stage-4-automation.md
!docs/paper-lifecycle-equivalence.json

